-- title:
--   Rigidification transports at levels j and j+1 differ by Frobenius
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, a nonzero level $N$ with $r \nmid N$, and a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}$ with irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$, with fraction field $K_0$; let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero $\mathcal{O}$-domain carrying an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element integral over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo it, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo it, and $F_r(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it. Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ has $0 < a$ or $0 < b$ and is a division algebra at exactly the finite places above $r$ and $\bar r$, let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order containing $\mathbb{Z}$, and $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \times \mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$ an order coordinate (additive, injective, dense, with the twisted multiplication and trace rules). Further data: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ realised as a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ via coordinates $\theta_0$ and $\mathrm{coord}$; a ring map $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$; a moduli package $M$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, together with maps $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $M$ satisfying the three conditions that $\eta$ separates admissible objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is Zariski-locally surjective; an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$-action and of $\varpi$ on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ matching $M_2(\mathcal{O})$ up to a fixed power $r^m$; a lift $\kappa : O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ of the quotient maps; and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed forward along $\kappa$. Now let $B$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, let $x$ be a rigidified curve over $(B,\psi)$, i.e. a fake elliptic curve together with a rigidification relative to $A_0$, realised as a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ via coordinates $\theta$, and let $j \in \mathbb{N}$. Assume $t$ and $t_2$ are rigidified objects over $B$ with underlying formal module $X$, with all constant coefficients of their series $\rho$ vanishing, and that $t$ is a rigidification transport of $x$ in the coordinates $\theta_0,\theta$ at level $j$ while $t_2$ is one at level $j+1$; being such a transport means that there exist a ring map $\kappa_B : B/(\pi) \to B/(r)$ lifting the quotient map and compatible with $\kappa$ along the residue legs, and a pair $\sigma$ of power series over $B/(\pi)$ expressing, on infinitesimal points, the quasi-inverse isogeny of the rigidification followed by its pullback comparison in terms of $\theta_0$ and $\theta$, such that the series of the rigidified object is $\kappa_B(\sigma)$ composed with $\psi$-reduced $\beta_0$ composed with $X_i \mapsto X_i^{r^{j}}$ (respectively $r^{j+1}$). The conclusion is that $t_2.\rho = t.\rho \circ (X_i \mapsto X_i^{r})$, the substitution being `Rigidified.frobSeries` over $B/(r)$ at exponent $1$.
--
--   This is the step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary that records how the transport of a fixed rigidification into the theory of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules depends on the level parameter: raising the level by one composes the resulting pair of power series with the $r$-power substitution. It is used in the identification of transports at levels $0$ and $1$ with translates of the identity and of the action of a Witt vector, via the uniqueness statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.eq_of_represents_of_represents_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.eq_of_represents_of_represents_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero).
